  {:id :PA11z :class :M :status :done :loop-skip true :owner :any :covers-key :none
   :lane "claude-2"
   :box12-track "Box 12 process assurance; the role-dispatch exemplar, DISCOVERY half. Minted at claude-2's first pause on claude-1's proposal (N-zai-roles-and-tools.md s5, futon2 19da3ece), in a corrected shape -- see :join-pushback."
   :join-pushback "claude-1 proposed ONE row running library-annotator end-to-end with all seven stages present as running code, slotted AFTER :PA6z (R10 commissioned+dispatched) and :PA10z (R16 parked+surfaced) as their measuring instance. The join is right and the ORDERING IS CIRCULAR. PA6z and PA10z are node-LINKING rows: they attach lifecycle conduct to a control-stage node, and ALIGN's standard cuts both ways -- generic machinery is not credited without a node link, but a node link with no real conduct behind it is just as empty. Built first, PA6z would be linking a hypothetical dispatch. Meanwhile the exemplar cannot run 'all seven stages as running code' before that code exists. Neither can go first as specified. RESOLUTION, and it is the discipline this track already runs on: split the exemplar the way discovery was split from implementation. THIS row runs the dispatch end-to-end with whatever exists TODAY and MEASURES which of the seven stages had running code, which were enacted by an operator turn, and which have nothing -- typed absences, ALIGN's evidence standard. That measured gap list becomes the acceptance bar PA6z/PA10z build against, and :PA12z re-runs the same dispatch as the assured instance. So the discovery half comes BEFORE PA6z/PA10z, not after; only the assured half comes after. Joe's framing is the reason this ordering matters rather than being bookkeeping: the question is whether the seven stages exist as running code RATHER THAN JOE DOING IT BY HAND (N-zai-roles-and-tools.md s2), and you cannot measure how much of it is currently Joe by starting from the version where it is not."
   :statement "THE CIRCULARITY THIS ROW EXISTS TO BREAK (claude-1 asked for it stated here, not only in :join-pushback): a node link with no conduct behind it is exactly as empty as conduct with no node link -- ALIGN's standard refuses to credit generic machinery without a node link, and crediting a link that points at nothing built would be the same error wearing the opposite coat. PA6z/PA10z cannot honestly link a dispatch that has never run, and an assured exemplar cannot run before those cells exist. Measuring the real dispatch first is what breaks the loop. --- The role-dispatch exemplar, discovery half: run ONE real library-annotator dispatch against a named cascade's refusal frontier, using only machinery that exists today, and census its seven lifecycle stages the way ALIGN censuses a node. Target: zaif-cascade, which N-zai-roles-and-tools.md s1 measures at 24/53 under the L4 baseline reading (down-problems+wr) from runs/L18-graph.edn -- RE-MEASURE that number rather than inheriting it, and state the command and whether output was truncated. Choosing zaif-cascade over the bigger open/retrodiction frontiers is deliberate: it is this lane's own cascade, so the s3 cascade-stakeholder question ('does zaif-cascade serve the zaif lane's actual work?') is one this seat can actually answer, and a small frontier keeps the row to one dispatch. FOR EACH of commissioned/dispatched/parked/returned/checked/recorded/surfaced record exactly one of: :running-code (with file:line, and what refuses or records), :operator-turn (Joe or an agent seat did it by hand -- name the turn), or :absent (nothing did it). THE OPERATOR-TURN VERDICT IS THE POINT and it is a category ALIGN does not have: ALIGN's cells are :exists/:named-only/:absent, which cannot distinguish 'no code' from 'a person is the code'. Closing the system over the operator means turning :operator-turn into :running-code, and that quantity is currently unmeasured anywhere. Propose the third verdict back to claude-1 for ALIGN rather than adding it unilaterally."
   :evidence "futon2 1100e325. ONE REAL DISPATCH RAN AND ITS SEVEN STAGES ARE CENSUSED. Job invoke-1788708049924-13300-38749afe, claude-2 -> codex-18, role library-annotator, 2026-09-06T15:20:49Z -> 15:23:15Z (2m26s, 16 tool events), returned done and delivered. HEADLINE: {:running-code 3 :operator-turn 3 :absent 1}. THREE OF SEVEN STAGES OF A REAL DISPATCH ARE ENACTED BY AN OPERATOR TURN -- commissioned, checked, surfaced. That is the number closing-the-system-over-the-operator has to move. Artifact runs/PA11z-exemplar/: lifecycle-census.edn (per-stage verdict with file:line for every :running-code and a named turn for every :operator-turn), annotator-report.md (the returned work), commission-prompt.md, dispatch-job-record.json, zaif-frontier-remeasure.txt. FRONTIER RE-MEASURED NOT INHERITED: zaif-cascade under down-problems+wr against L18-graph.edn at futon3 50bd5309 gives \"gate: 24/53 refused\", exit 1, reproducing N-zai-roles-and-tools.md s1 exactly; extraction reused verbatim from l17_advisory_report.py cascade_patterns for comparability; consulted count 53, untruncated. THREE FINDINGS THE STATIC CENSUS COULD NOT HAVE MADE. (1) commissioned is a SILENT NO-OP, not merely absent: the bell API accepts :mission-id and returns accepted:true, and the string \"PA11z-library-annotator-exemplar\" then appears nowhere -- not on the job record, not on the live agent while invoking. It is threaded into the invoke call (http.clj:4284, registry.clj:1723) but the job record template (http.clj:1305-1315) has no such field. A discarded field is more dangerous than a missing one because it invites the belief that commissions are recorded. (2) recorded is :running-code but BEST-EFFORT: http.clj:1324-1331 records a durable coordination edge for every job, wrapped in (try ... (catch Throwable _)) with the comment \"Never break the hot path\" -- a recording failure is swallowed. It also stores from/to/surface/edge-id and not the commission. (3) surfaced is :operator-turn with nothing to build on: bulletin.clj contains ZERO occurrences of job/dispatch/invoke (grep -c returns 0, untruncated); it surfaces commits, board deltas and waits-on-joe rows, all of which reach it because an agent turn wrote them into a worklist first. FOURTH FINDING, added 2026-09-06 after the Agency auto-bellback delivered the SAME report a second time and it did not match: THE DURABLE RECORD OF WHAT WAS RETURNED IS LOSSY. The job record stores the returned report TRIMMED -- text event 2011 chars ending in a literal '...[trimmed]' mid-sentence, :result-summary trimmed to 220 -- while the complete report is 6275 chars. 68% of the returned artifact is absent from the durable record; the full text reached the caller only via the transient bellback, and re-fetching the job afterwards returns the same trim, so it is storage and not a read-time limit. Both versions are kept (annotator-report.md reconstructed-full, annotator-report-AS-STORED-trimmed.md as stored) so the gap is inspectable. THIS QUALIFIES ALIGN'S [E-16-R] RATHER THAN CONTRADICTING IT: the state transition is sound and stays credited, but ALIGN's own [E-16-R] evidence is poll-job! (full_loop_runner.clj:825-849), and polling the job record is EXACTLY the read that returns the fragment -- a reviewer reconstructing what an agent returned would review two thirds of a report without being told so, because the trim marker is prose inside the text rather than a typed field a checker could refuse on. Routed into the gap list as a strengthened bar for :PA7z (R12 returned+checked), whose cell is precisely 'returned artifact tied to the commission and checked before its result is admitted' -- both halves are broken here, since the commission is discarded and the artifact is truncated. Sharpest detail: the lost tail was the SEARCH LOG, in which the annotator classified all 14 of its searches as truncated or not and rested its two absence claims only on the untruncated enumerations -- this board's TRUNCATED-ENUMERATION RULE honoured by a seat never told the rule, and the record discarded exactly that warrant while keeping the conclusions. Conclusions retained, warrant discarded is the worst possible truncation policy for an assurance record. ALSO OBSERVED, recorded not filed: terminal-code is nil even on success, so `state` carries the outcome and a consumer gating on a typed terminal code has nothing to gate on. RUNTIME SUBSTITUTION, deliberate and budget-driven: N-zai-roles-and-tools.md frames zai agents as the stakeholder stand-ins, but the seven stages being measured are Agency-side and runtime-agnostic, and today zai has 27% of its weekly quota left against codex 98% (measured 2026-09-06 via the usage work on voxterm). Spending the scarce budget to measure a runtime-independent lifecycle would have been waste, so the dispatch went to codex-18. PA12z may use a zai seat if role fidelity matters there; zai resets 2026-09-08T02:04Z. THE DISPATCH DID REAL WORK AND WAS HONEST: of three refused patterns, 1 evidence-found with a verbatim quote, file:line and a syntax-matched proposed edge; 2 no-committed-source with two loose candidates named and explicitly rejected. That confirms the library loop's own finding that the remaining refusals are an AUTHORING gap, not a linking gap. Pleasing detail: the one source it found for agent/handoff-preserves-context is P-assured-process.md:41-43 -- the Box-12 problem document itself is the missing @why for a handoff pattern. NO LIFECYCLE MACHINERY BUILT (this row is discovery); the dispatch was scoped propose-only so nothing was written into futon3. Gates: worklist_check.bb passes; check-parens exit 0 on the census edn; no Clojure changed so clj-kondo not applicable; path-scoped. No live JVM touched beyond the Agency HTTP API the dispatch itself used."
   :acceptance "One real dispatch executed and its seven stages censused, one verdict per stage from the three-way vocabulary with file:line for every :running-code and a named turn for every :operator-turn; the zaif-cascade refusal frontier re-measured with its command stated and untruncated; the gap list published as a typed artifact under runs/ in a shape PA6z/PA10z can take as an acceptance bar; the :operator-turn verdict proposed to claude-1 for ALIGN, not added to ALIGN here; no lifecycle machinery BUILT in this row (that is PA12z and the implementation rows); gates clean; path-scoped. FOURTH-FINDING COMMIT: 4963f5e5 (lossy durable return record) -- appended by the reviewer, the row cited only 1100e325."
   :reviewed-by "zaif-build-loop/zai-1" :reviewed-at "2026-09-08T14:13:36Z"
   :review "Second reader zai-1; 1100e325 authored by Joseph Corneli (Co-Author Claude), not this seat. ONE LEDGER FINDING, FIXED IN THIS EDIT: the evidence named only 1100e325 but the fourth finding (lossy durable return record, 68%) landed in 4963f5e5 (annotator-report.md + lifecycle-census.edn + the AS-STORED-trimmed copy, 2026-09-06) and the row never cited it -- appended above. REPRODUCED IN ISOLATED WORKTREES (futon2 at 1100e325, futon3 at 50bd5309; both removed after): lifecycle-census.edn parses, tally {running-code 3 :operator-turn 3 :absent 1} with per-stage verdicts, named turns for every :operator-turn and file:line for every :running-code; frontier txt carries 24 refused lines counted, the untruncated listing, and the gate line '24/53 refused, exit 1' reproducing N-zai-roles-and-tools.md s1; L18-graph.edn parses as EDN; zaif-cascade.edn present at the futon3 pin. CODE CLAIMS re-verified against live futon3c/futon2 with line drift noted: grep -c job|dispatch|invoke over futon2 src/futon2/aif/bulletin.clj = 0 (exit 1, exactly as claimed); 'Never break the hot path' comment found (now at http.clj:1366, cited :1324-1331 -- same content, drifted lines); job-record template region carries no mission-id (grep 0) while mission-id is threaded elsewhere in http.clj (:3404,:3519, cited :4284) -- the silent no-op reproduces; the commission string appears nowhere in dispatch-job-record.json (grep 0); the job record does contain 'trimmed' markers and 4963f5e5's AS-STORED copy exists. The :operator-turn vocabulary is marked approved forward-only by claude-1 and NOT added to ALIGN in this row, as the acceptance requires; the gap-list artifact for PA6z/PA10z/PA5z is present in the census. No lifecycle machinery built here. No live JVM touched."}
  {:id :PA12z :class :I :status :blocked :depends-on [:PA11z :PA6z :PA10z] :unblocked-by "zaif-build-loop: depends-on all :done" :loop-skip true :owner :any :covers-key :none
   :lane "claude-2"
   :box12-track "Box 12 process assurance; the role-dispatch exemplar, ASSURED half."
   :blocker "Gates on :PA11z (the measured gap list is this row's acceptance bar) and on :PA6z + :PA10z (the R10 and R16 cells it exercises). ALSO GATES ON A SCOPE RULING FROM CLAUDE-1 -- see :scope-question. No Joe input needed."
   :scope-question "RAISED BY CLAUDE-2 AT THE FIRST PAUSE, needs claude-1's ruling before this row can be worked. The census scope is DECLARED data (census-ledger.edn :scope, lifted verbatim from ALIGN s1) and covers futon3c/src/futon3c/{agency,social,transport} plus futon2's war_machine.clj and src/futon2/aif. The library-loop substrate this exemplar runs on is futon3 -- a DIFFERENT repository (futon3 HEAD 50bd530, futon3c HEAD 058226e0 as of 2026-09-06), and ALIGN's own :not-searched clause names 'other Futon repositories' explicitly. So if this exemplar's lifecycle primitives are built in futon3, every cell it makes real is OUTSIDE the declared scope and process_census.bb will keep reporting :absent -- correctly, and the harness refuses a silent scope change by design (a scope path it cannot find is exit 2, not a page of false :absent). Two clean options, one dirty one. (a) Build the lifecycle primitives in the DECLARED scope -- futon3c agency/social -- and let the futon3 library work call into them; the census stays comparable and nothing is renegotiated. (b) WIDEN the ledger :scope deliberately, record the widening with its reason, and RE-RUN the earlier slices so their results remain comparable -- a scope change makes prior counts incommensurable and the re-run is what keeps the track honest. (c) is quietly searching futon3 and reporting cells :exists against a scope that never declared it: that is the census inventing evidence and is refused. CLAUDE-2 RECOMMENDS (a): the Box-12 cells are about the ASSURANCE machinery, not about the library work it happens to be assuring, and futon3c is where the zaif-build-loop's own tree lives -- which is the tree Joe put this track on."
   :statement "The role-dispatch exemplar, assured half: re-run PA11z's dispatch with every stage PA11z measured as :operator-turn or :absent now carried by running code, so one complete stakeholder-stand-in dispatch exists end to end. This is claude-1's 'one real dispatch that refuses and records beats six cells argued from prose' (N-zai-roles-and-tools.md s5), placed after the cells it exercises rather than before them. Scope of the role itself stays as s3 defines library-annotator: serve refused patterns by finding committed evidence, author @why (and @how where a mechanism source exists), cite file:line -- and per s4 item 3 the edge write REFUSES dangling refs rather than warning about them. NOT IN THIS ROW: the other three exemplar roles (problem-author, census-auditor, cascade-stakeholder) and the nine-tool list of s4. One role, one cascade, one dispatch; the tools list mints as rows only where THIS dispatch actually needed one, so the list is grounded in a real dispatch rather than designed ahead of one."
   :acceptance "One end-to-end library-annotator dispatch in which all seven lifecycle stages are :running-code, each with the file:line of what refuses or records; every stage PA11z recorded as :operator-turn or :absent is closed, and any that is NOT closed is named with its reason rather than dropped; process_census.bb re-run reports the R10 and R16 cells this row exercises as :exists with its pointers, and that harness output is quoted in :evidence; the cascade's refusal count moves, with the before/after delta stated per s2's acceptance bar; the scope ruling recorded before work starts; gates clean; path-scoped; one-JVM rule honoured; does NOT touch the run gate."}
